tual root cause.\r\n\r\nCheck:\r\n\r\n- Email service integration\r\n- Email provider configuration\r\n- Environment variables\r\n- SMTP/API configuration\r\n- Notification trigger logic\r\n- Bill reminder scheduling\r\n- Pantry low-stock notification logic\r\n- Background/scheduled jobs\r\n- Authenticated user's email retrieval\r\n- Email delivery errors\r\n- Server-side logs and error handling\r\n\r\nIMPORTANT:\r\n\r\n- Emails must actually be delivered.\r\n- Do NOT simulate email delivery.\r\n- Do NOT create fake success messages.\r\n- Do NOT expose API keys or SMTP credentials.\r\n- Keep all secrets server-side in environment variables.\r\n- Do not remove existing notification functionality.\r\n\r\nIf a required email provider credential/configuration is missing, clearly identify exactly what is required instead of creating a fake implementation.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 3. FIX UI SO DATA UPDATES WITHOUT MANUAL REFRESH\r\n\r\nCurrently, after actions such as:\r\n\r\n- Add bill\r\n- Delete bill\r\n- Add expense\r\n- Delete expense\r\n- Change pantry quantity\r\n- Add/remove pantry items\r\n- Update budget\r\n- Other existing CRUD operations\r\n\r\nthe database changes but the visible UI does not update until I manually refresh the browser.\r\n\r\nFix the actual state/data synchronization issue.\r\n\r\nExpected behavior:\r\n\r\nUser action\r\n→ Database/backend operation succeeds\r\n→ Application state/data updates\r\n→ UI immediately reflects the change\r\n→ No manual browser refresh required\r\n\r\nInspect the existing:\r\n\r\n- Frontend state management\r\n- API calls\r\n- Data fetching\r\n- Mutation handling\r\n- Caching\r\n- Database queries\r\n- Component updates\r\n\r\nDo NOT solve this by forcing a full-page reload after every action.\r\n\r\nAfter fixing it, verify that:\r\n\r\n- Added data appears immediately\r\n- Deleted data disappears immediately\r\n- Updated values appear immediately\r\n- Dashboard totals update immediately\r\n- Budget calculations update immediately\r\n- Pie charts update when underlying data changes\r\n- Notifications/alerts update appropriately\r\n\r\nDo not break existing CRUD functionality.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 4. ADD PKR AS DEFAULT CURRENCY\r\n\r\nThe application currently supports multiple currencies, but Pakistani Rupee is missing.\r\n\r\nMake this targeted currency change:\r\n\r\n- Add Pakistani Rupee (PKR) as a supported currency.\r\n- Make PKR the DEFAULT currency.\r\n- New users should have PKR selected by default.\r\n- Display PKR consistently throughout the application.\r\n- Bills must support PKR.\r\n- Expenses must support PKR.\r\n- Budgets must support PKR.\r\n- Pantry spending must support PKR.\r\n- Totals and remaining amounts must support PKR.\r\n- Summaries must support PKR.\r\n- Pie charts must correctly display PKR-related financial data.\r\n- Keep all currently supported currencies.\r\n- Do NOT remove existing currencies.\r\n- Use the application's existing currency system rather than creating a separate one.\r\n- Ensure PKR formatting is handled correctly.\r\n\r\nDo NOT make unrelated UI changes.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS\r\n\r\nThese are TARGETED FIXES ONLY.\r\n\r\nDO NOT:\r\n\r\n- Rebuild the application\r\n- Redesign the UI\r\n- Change the existing visual design\r\n- Remove existing features\r\n- Simplify existing functionality\r\n- Add unrelated features\r\n- Replace working components unnecessarily\r\n- Replace the existing architecture without a genuine technical reason\r\n- Use dummy data\r\n- Use fake APIs\r\n- Simulate email delivery\r\n- Hardcode API keys\r\n- Hardcode production credentials\r\n- Break authentication\r\n- Break the database\r\n- Remove existing currencies\r\n- Create placeholder implementations\r\n\r\nPreserve everything that is already working.\r\n\r\nBefore changing anything, inspect the existing code and identify the root cause of each issue.\r\n\r\nAfter making the changes, actually test the application.\r\n\r\nDo NOT say something is fixed merely because the code compiles.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## FINAL VERIFICATION\r\n\r\nBefore declaring the task complete, verify:\r\n\r\n[ ] `node server/index.js` starts successfully.\r\n\r\n[ ] The existing server/API routes still work.\r\n\r\n[ ] CORS still works.\r\n\r\n[ ] Real email notification functionality works or any genuinely missing external credential/configuration is clearly identified.\r\n\r\n[ ] Bill reminders use the existing notification system correctly.\r\n\r\n[ ] Pantry low-stock notifications work correctly.\r\n\r\n[ ] Adding/deleting/updating data immediately updates the UI without browser refresh.\r\n\r\n[ ] Dashboard totals update immediately.\r\n\r\n[ ] Budget calculations update immediately.\r\n\r\n[ ] Pie charts update when underlying data changes.\r\n\r\n[ ] PKR exists as a supported currency.\r\n\r\n[ ] PKR is the default currency.\r\n\r\n[ ] Existing currencies remain available.\r\n\r\n[ ] Existing authentication continues working.\r\n\r\n[ ] Existing database functionality continues working.\r\n\r\n[ ] No dummy/fake functionality has been introduced.\r\n\r\n[ ] No unrelated changes have been made.\r\n\r\nIMPORTANT: Work with the EXISTING application and make only these targeted fixes.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-03T08:39:05-07:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\n<USER_SETTINGS_CHANGE>\nThe user changed setting `Model Selection` from Claude Sonnet 4.6 (Thinking) to Gemini 3.8 Flash (High). No need to comment on this change if the user doesn't ask about it. If reporting what model you are, please use a human readable name instead of the exact string.\n</USER_SETTINGS_CHANGE>"}
